menu "Station: bench console (bench builds only)"

    config BENCH_CONSOLE
        bool "Bench console on the UART0 console (never in a release)"
        depends on ESP_CONSOLE_UART
        default n
        select UM98X_FLASH_BYTE_CAPTURE
        help
            A command line on the UART0 console (115200, alongside the log)
            that drives the receiver flasher's bench tests one at a time:
            listen only, the version query, the loader entry probe, the menu
            item 2 probe, the loader idle observation, the stop key from
            boot (armed for one boot), a full same-build flash, a deliberate
            abort, and the journal-state helper. Every command that writes
            to the receiver asks for a typed confirmation word, runs through
            the station's normal ownership of the receiver link (casters
            paused, refused in maintenance and while anything else runs),
            records every byte (also downloadable from the web UI's
            Logs > Console) and prints a PASS/FAIL line. Nothing runs at boot
            except the one-shot stop key, and only when armed. The release
            job refuses a build with this on.

            The command line reads the console UART through the driver the
            log tap installs at boot (it never installs a second one), and
            its replies go out through the log's console writer a whole
            line at a time, so a log line never lands inside one.

endmenu
